# Level 9 -> Level 10

# Objective:
Retrieve the password for bandit10 stored in data.txt as a human-readable string preceded by several = characters.

# breakdown:
The file data.txt contains binary data mixed with printable text.
 Running strings extracts all printable ASCII strings, and piping (|) the stream into grep -E "={2,}" filters the output to display only lines containing consecutive = characters.

Command:
strings data.txt | grep -E "={2,}"
